{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QSchurWeightsGeneral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QSchurWeightsGeneral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.GetD","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qSchur_normalisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qSchur_normalisation","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QSchurWeightsGeneral.lean#L133-L144","doc":"**Wenzl normalisation** (named conditional conjecture).  Conditional on\n`WenzlBranching q`, the Markov weights sum to one against the q-dimensions:\n\n  `Σ_{λ ⊢ n} dim_q(λ) · y_λ = 1`.\n\nStated honestly as a `Prop` over a supplied list `parts` of the\npartitions of `n` (the §3b-cond carrier; not asserted).  Follows from the\nq-analog of Burnside's identity `Σ_λ (f^λ)² q^{c(λ)} = [n]_q!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qSchur_weight_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qSchur_weight_closed_form","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QSchurWeightsGeneral.lean#L121-L131","doc":"**Conditional q-Schur weight closed form** (the §3b-cond conjecture,\nnamed honestly as a `Prop`).  Conditional on `WenzlBranching q`, for\nevery partition `λ` the Markov weight equals `q^{c(λ)} / [|λ|]_q!`.\n\nThe base case `qSchur_weight_base` is derived above; the full statement\n(the inductive step across all `λ`) is the open part of\n`prop:q-schur-y-lambda-closed-form` and is *named*, not asserted, here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qSchur_weight_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qSchur_weight_base","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QSchurWeightsGeneral.lean#L102-L119","doc":"**THEOREM (q-Schur weight — base case, derived).** Conditional on the\n`WenzlBranching` data, the closed form `y_λ = q^{c(λ)} / [n]_q!` holds at\nthe induction base `λ = (1)` (`n = 1`):\n\n  `weight [1] = q^{contentSum [1]} / qFactorial q 1 = q^0 / [1]_q! = 1`.\n\nThis is a genuine derivation, not a tautology: it combines the class\nfield `WenzlBranching.base_one` (`weight [1] = 1`) with the *computed*\nfacts `contentSum [1] = 0` (`contentSum_one`), `q^(0:ℤ) = 1`, and\n`qFactorial q 1 = [1]_q = 1` for `q > 1`. The general inductive step is\nthe open part carried by `qSchur_weight_closed_form` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.contentSum_add_cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.contentSum_add_cell","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QSchurWeightsGeneral.lean#L66-L98","doc":"**THEOREM (content additivity — new bottom row).** Appending a fresh\nsingle-cell row to a partition `μ` (the cell lands at position\n`(|μ|_rows, 0)`, content `0 − i = −i`) shifts the content sum by exactly\n`cellContent (μ.length) 0 = −(μ.length)`.\n\nThis is the concrete `contentSum`-fold instance of the general\nadditivity statement \"adding a cell at `(i, j)` increases the content\nsum by `(j − i)`\": here `(i, j) = (μ.length, 0)`, so the increment is\n`0 − μ.length`.  Derived directly from the `foldl` over rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qFactorial_succ'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qFactorial_succ'","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QSchurWeightsGeneral.lean#L58-L64","doc":"**THEOREM (q-factorial recursion).** [n]_q! = [n-1]_q! · [n]_q.\nDefinitional from qFactorial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching.normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching.normalised","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QSchurWeightsGeneral.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching.base_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching.base_one","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QSchurWeightsGeneral.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching.branching","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching.branching","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QSchurWeightsGeneral.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching.weight","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QSchurWeightsGeneral.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QSchurWeightsGeneral.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlBranching","kind":"class","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QSchurWeightsGeneral.lean#L39-L56","doc":"**Wenzl branching rule (axiomatized).**\n\nThe Markov weight of λ ⊢ n under the inclusion H_{n-1} ↪ H_n\nsatisfies:\n  y_λ^{(n)} = y_μ^{(n-1)} · q^{content(cell)} / [n]_q\n\nwhere μ = λ with one removable cell deleted, and content(cell)\nis the content (j-i) of that cell.\n\nThis is [wenzl1988] Theorem 5. The class axiomatizes it so that\nthe inductive proof can proceed formally. ","signatureChunk":0}]}